{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/21398-what-are-some-good-hobgoblins-to-join-a-freehold","id":21398,"title":"What are some Good Hobgoblins to join a Freehold?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-01T19:00:03-08:00","id":21398,"title":"What are some Good Hobgoblins to join a Freehold?","content":"Okay more on the subject of bolstering Freehold numbers, I like to use enchanted Mortals and Fetches but Hobgoblins would also do the trick. So does anyone have good suggestions for Hobgoblins that would work fine as members of a Freehold? They can be either from a book, or purely homebrewed. I forgot but wasn't their some instances of Hobgoblin's gaining Mantles?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking they would be in a freehold hold that has at least one Communal Hallow, so they can live in or around it, but also what about Hobgoblins in the mortal world? The books seem to shy away from this but they have some that interact with the mortal world. The Domovoi from Proverbial monsters is one example, and they seem actually like they might work as a workable type of Hobgoblin that could live in a Freehold.<br /> <br /> There is that freehold merit for making I think Automaton Hobgoblins, that is something I've used as a potential use for merits once a shared hallow maxes out, such as when you have a Freehold with a shared Hallow that all members buy at least one dot in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:41:32-08:00","id":22007,"title":"","content":"I've got a blunderbore NPC in the freehold. He's the resident pacifist handyman. It's in the early stages of the game just yet, and he hasn't made an entrance, but will soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1386-thompry","name":"thompry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1386_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T20:46:52-08:00","id":22096,"title":"","content":"My Freehold has a wandering Butcherbranch. Not really a resident, he's sort of the local Hedge's home meal delivery service, but I could see one fitting into a Freehold ok. They do make Glamour recovery spectacularly easy though, so if you want resource scarcity to be a thing in your game I really don't recommend it. The one in my game has a habit of tearing through the local Goblin Fruit groves and not leaving much for anyone else. Since one of my players has a large grove that he's been carefully cultivating in his Hollow, it came as a bit of a rude surprise when this enormous toad-thing wandered in and started taking everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T11:04:43-08:00","id":22448,"title":"","content":"One thing that seems likely to come up in my campaign soon is the idea of Hobgoblin &quot;contractors.&quot; Hobs are mercenary by nature, and plenty of other hobgoblins might accept some kind of deal that goes &quot;you work for the Freehold, we give you glamour/other nice things.&quot; In my case, there might be some hobgoblins who'll be keep an eye on a Hedge-river. <br /> <br /> You might also consider Hedge Beasts. Plenty of them hang out with changelings as is, no reason that can't be scaled up a bit. Sure, the Hedge Beast tiger doesn't want anything from any individual changeling, but there's probably something it wants from a Freehold as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T17:36:36-08:00","id":31352,"title":"","content":"Did we ever actually get any specific rules on Hobgoblins outside the Hedge? It feels like we should have but I don't remember any, it just seemed like they preferred to stay in the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:51:45-08:00","id":31402,"title":"","content":"I think it varies from Hobgoblin to Hobgoblin. Autumn Nightmares has a tribe of creatures called the Border Reavers, which evidently can leave the Hedge (and have done so many times in the past) but mutate horribly every time they leave it. I think there are one or two creatures in the same book (Drudgemen come to mind) which are described as interacting with humans on some level. So I guess it just depends on the type.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just checked. Autumn Nightmares has a small section called &quot;Hobgoblins and the Hedge&quot; which includes a paragraph of how and why a Hobgoblin might leave the Hedge. It even says that some Hobgoblins might manage to carve out a niche for themselves within a Lost Court, or even the Mortal world if gifted with the ability to pass themselves off as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 12-16-2013, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}